+# Panel review — claude seat, 2026-10-05 (joint/star round)
+
+Every figure below was produced by execution in this review. Producers are named per
+figure and are committed alongside this file. **I do not recommend the proposal as
+written, and the reason is a defect in the instrument it would promote.**
+
+## The instrument is arithmetically wrong, and the error alone inverts the ladder
+
+`scripts/competence_provenance.py` is the check `bench/routing.py`'s star-marked
+founder observation names as the thing that must run before the order is re-derived,
+and §2 of this proposal would promote it from a record to a **gate on pool entry**. It
+keyed every falsifier on the entry's `source_model`.
+
+`reference_runner_v3`'s routing block, in its `elif result.resolved:` arm, does:
+
+```
+e["falsifier_code"] = result.falsifier_code      # the RESOLVING RUNG's falsifier
+e["falsifier_verdict"] = "CONFIRMED"
+e["resolved_by_routing"] = result.model_used     # who actually wrote it
+```
+
+so on every routed resolution the falsifier is replaced by the resolver's and
+`source_model` still names the model whose own falsifier failed.
+
+Measured over 72 archived reports by
+`scripts/the_provenance_gate_credits_the_wrong_model_2026-10-05.py`:
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| registry entries | 3036 |
+| resolved by the routing ladder | 248 |
+| …of which CONFIRMED | 248 (100%) |
+| credited to the wrong model | **248 = 8.169%** |
+
+Every misattributed entry is a **confirmation**, so the whole error sits in the
+numerator of the rate §1 defines, and it always moves credit **from a resolver to a
+source** — the same direction as the selection effect this proposal names as its
+strongest objection. They compound; they do not cancel.
+
+Effect on the only thing that matters, the induced ordering of the 5 real vendors:
+
+| basis | induced order | Kendall τ vs frozen |
+|---|---|---|
+| frozen `DEFAULT_FALSIFIER_STRENGTH` | Codex, CC2, ChatGPT, Gemini, DeepSeek | — |
+| **keyed on `source_model` (the defect)** | Gemini, Codex, ChatGPT, DeepSeek, CC2 | **0.0000** |
+| keyed on the falsifier's author | Codex, Gemini, CC2, ChatGPT, DeepSeek | **+0.6000** |
+
+τ by scipy `kendalltau`; independently confirmed by Wolfram Language (local Wolfram
+Engine via `wolframscript`): `{0, 0.6}`. Under the defect the instrument has **zero
+rank correlation** with the Exp-42 measurement it would displace, and it puts **CC2 —
+rung 2 of the validated ladder — last, below DeepSeek**.
+
+**Repaired here**, minimally and additively: `competence_provenance.falsifier_author`
+keys on `resolved_by_routing or source_model`, every non-routed entry keeps its
+historical attribution, and the reattribution count is printed per model so a reader
+can see why a number moved. Pinned by
+`bench/tests/test_provenance_credits_the_falsifier_author_2026-10-05.py` (8 tests).
+The 13 pre-existing pinned tests in
+`test_defect_rate_and_competence_provenance_2026-08-23.py` still pass.
+
+Note what the repair does **not** fix: the corrected rate still ranks **Gemini second**,
+and Gemini is the model the Exp-55 detachment measurement indicts. So the
+reads/detached gate remains necessary and the attribution fix does not substitute for
+it. That is a *demonstrated* composition of two fixes, not an assumed one.
+
+## The ladder's direction is specified twice in `bench/routing.py`, incompatibly
+
+This is why two seats and CC1 reached opposite verdicts on the simulated seat map, and
+the disagreement is not about evidence.
+
+* **Statement A**, module docstring: route "to progressively **STRONGER** models" —
+  rung 1 is the weakest tried. The docstring's own Exp-42 account sides with A
+  explicitly: rung 1 is gpt-5.5 (Codex) at 6/7, and "the remaining one … is resolved
+  by the next, **stronger** rung (opus-class)".
+* **Statement B**, `rank_falsifier_writers`: "ordered **strongest-first**", with Codex
+  at index 0 — rung 1 is the strongest tried.
+
+Codex is therefore at once the strongest model and weaker than the model at the next
+rung. **The code is coherent** — the tuple is ordered by Exp-42 *confirm rate*, which
+the comment states, and confirm rate is not generic capability. It is the docstring's
+word "STRONGER" that is unbacked, and it sits in the same sentence as "ordered by
+capability fingerprint", which this proposal shows the code never reads. **One
+sentence, two claims the code does not make; the proposal caught one.**
+
+Measured by `scripts/the_ladder_direction_is_stated_twice_2026-10-05.py`:
+
+| seat map | mixed | descending (B) | ascending (A) |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| CC1 shipped, budget 4 | 6/6 | **6/6** | 0/6 |
+| fable seat's map, budget 2 | 5/6 | 0/6 | **5/6** |
+
+Each map is the faithful one under one reading. `test_the_exercised_ladder_prefix_is_
+mixed_2026-10-05.py` asserts "no weaker model appears before a stronger one", which
+**freezes reading B** and falsifies the other seat's map on that basis — without the
+ambiguity being recorded anywhere. Recorded now, in `bench/routing.py` at the point of
+the tuple. Nothing removed; which sentence is the specification is a founder call, and
+whichever wins, the other has to go.
+
+**This bears directly on the proposal.** §1 defines a rate and §4 would rank on it,
+implicitly highest-first. If reading A is the design intent, confirm rate is not just a
+noisy key — it is the wrong *axis*, and no amount of provenance gating fixes that.
+**The proposal must state which direction it is ordering, and on what evidence.**
+
+## Answers to the four open questions
+
+1. **Is the construct right?** No, not as a replacement — and the numbers above make
+   this stronger than §"It may measure the wrong construct" states. Exp 42 measured
+   residual resolution directly on a fixed set (0/7 weak → 6/7 rung 1 → 7/7 rung 2).
+   The rate instrument, as shipped, disagreed with that measurement at τ = 0 for
+   bookkeeping reasons alone. Under the additive standard a measurement of a different
+   construct, by an instrument that was wrong until tonight, cannot displace a
+   committed measurement of the right one. **Rate as tripwire, Exp-42-style
+   fixed-residual probe as decider.**
+2. **Selection-effect mitigation.** First-pass-only is *not* sufficient and its stated
+   premise ("a common population by construction") is false — each model writes
+   first-pass falsifiers for *its own* findings, and the finding populations differ at
+   χ² = 280.0138, p = 2.213e-59. It also measures the wrong construct: demonstration
+   of own findings, not resolution of others' residuals. Use a **randomised audit
+   fraction of rung assignments** and compute the shadow statistic on randomised
+   attempts only. That is the only candidate that measures the ladder's own construct
+   on an assignment independent of the ranking.
+3. **Bundling with `immune_memory_enabled`.** No. Shared Beta-Binomial machinery is a
+   convenience, not a demonstrated advantage of the composed work over either fix
+   alone, and the composability standard requires the latter.
+4. **Glossary vs implementation.** Correct the glossary first, because it is the
+   cheaper half and because a documented dimension that does not exist is what let the
+   docstring's "ordered by capability fingerprint" go unchallenged for four months.
+
+## The simulated-launcher gap is 13 facilities, not 3
+
+Measured across 47 real experiment configs under `bench/exp*_configs/` against the
+AST of `run_simulated_experiment.py`. Fields armed non-default in ≥1 real config and
+absent from the simulated launcher:
+
+| field | real configs arming it |
+|---|---|
+| `context_files` | 47 of 47 |
+| `wall_clock_cap_s` | 45 of 47 |
+| `immune_memory_enabled` | 13 of 47 |
+| **`panel_cwd`** | **12 of 47** |
+| `target_kind` | 6 of 47 |
+| `hardened_gate_enabled` | 4 of 47 |
+| `exhausted_round_threshold` | 3 of 47 |
+| `feedback_channel_enabled` | 2 of 47 |
+| `divergence_channel_enabled` | 2 of 47 |
+| `gamma_alt_consecutive_zero_crit` | 1 of 47 |
+| `apply_fixes_back_enabled` | 1 of 47 |
+| `gamma_alt_threshold` | 1 of 47 |
+| `location_shadow_enabled` | 1 of 47 |
+
+Caveat, stated rather than papered over: "absent" means the simulated launcher takes
+the `RunnerConfig` default, which for the booleans is off and for `panel_cwd` /
+`context_files` / `wall_clock_cap_s` is unset. Some may be legitimately inapplicable.
+
+The three CC1 found are in the list, and the ones it missed are larger. **`panel_cwd`
+is the falsifier-integrity confinement control** — the CDSFL directive names it as one
+of four mechanical defences against a falsifier reaching outside the artefact — and it
+is unset in every simulated run, so that control has never been rehearsed.
+`wall_clock_cap_s` is armed by 45 of 47 real configs and unset in simulation, so the
+timeout path is unrehearsed on the same night a producer was written about a seat
+timing out.
+
+**`burst_mode="off"` is defensible, and more clearly than the other seat allowed.**
+Measured: 43 of 47 real configs set `burst_mode="off"`; 4 set `"auto"`; the
+`RunnerConfig` default is `"auto"`. So the simulated launcher's `"off"` is *parity with
+91.5% of real configs*, explicitly chosen against the default. The real gap is that the
+4-config `"auto"` path is unrehearsed — the same class as the ladder gap, an order of
+magnitude smaller.
