+
+## On the selection effect (open question 2) — first-pass-only is insufficient, and the reason is in this project's own χ²
+
+Mitigation 2 is defended here as giving "a common population by construction". It does
+not. Each model writes first-pass falsifiers for **its own** findings, and the finding
+populations differ per model — the project's own measurement, χ² = 280.0138, df = 4,
+p = 2.213e-59, is direct evidence that they do. First-pass-only therefore swaps a
+routing confound for a self-selection confound, and the construct it measures is
+"demonstrates its own findings", not "resolves what others could not".
+
+The fable seat proposed a randomised audit fraction of rung assignments. That is the
+right identification strategy and it is **not deployable at the scale this ladder
+runs**. Routing fires only on un-confirmed criticals; `routing_max_rungs` is 2; and
+rung 1 resolved 6 of 7 on the Exp-42 residual set. A randomised fraction of an already
+rare event yields a sample that will not reach any usable minimum-sample threshold
+within the project's run cadence. Randomisation identifies and does not estimate.
+
+**What is deployable, and it needs no new estimator.** The Exp-42 instrument is a
+*fixed residual set* — the hardest un-resolved criticals, held constant, re-run against
+each candidate rung. That is the ladder's construct measured directly, on a common
+population by construction rather than by assumption, and it is what Exp 42 did. The
+supported design is therefore: continuous rate as **drift detector only** (mitigation
+4), alarm triggers a **re-run of the fixed-residual probe**, and only the probe
+reorders. Rate = tripwire, probe = decider.
+
+## On the provenance gate (open question 2, §2) — it is not sufficient, and one of its defects is in the attribution, not the classifier
+
+Two defects, both executed, both now repaired in `scripts/competence_provenance.py`.
+
+1. **It credited the wrong model.** `analyse` keyed per-model on `source_model`, the
+   model that REPORTED the finding. When routing resolves a critical, the attached
+   falsifier was written by a ladder **rung**, which the runner records on the entry as
+   `resolved_by_routing`. Measured over this repository's archive: **1370 of 16500
+   registry entries carry `resolved_by_routing`** (8.3%), and every one had its
+   falsifier's provenance credited to the model that failed to write a working one.
+   The error runs in the direction that matters — a strong rung's successful
+   resolutions were credited to the weak source model, so the statistic protecting the
+   ladder's ordering flattered precisely the models the ladder demotes. This proposal's
+   §1 defines its numerator as "falsifiers **it** supplied", which is the rung, not the
+   source; the script it names as the gate implemented something else. The runner
+   already carried the correct precedence in `_corrected_copy_owner`.
+
+2. **The UNSAFE rule aggregated per model, not per confirmation.** Executed: 2 detached
+   CONFIRMED entries plus 1 reading REFUTED entry gave `reads == 1`, so `unsafe` was
+   False and a wholly detached pool passed. Now asked per confirmation. (Raised by the
+   fable seat; reproduced independently here.)
+
+**What neither repair fixes, and §2 must say so.** `falsifier_style` is a regex over
+text. Executed: `open("/dev/null")` → `reads`; the word `open(` in a **comment** →
+`reads`; a docstring mentioning `read_text` → `reads`. Gating pool entry on this script
+establishes that a falsifier contains the *vocabulary* of reading, not that it read
+anything. The hole is not closable by a better regex. Only execution-derived provenance
+closes it — an audit hook recording files opened during `reverify_falsifier`, or
+invariance of the verdict under a perturbed target. §2's claim that the gate "becomes a
+gate on pool entry" should be amended to state that the gate as written is necessary
+and not sufficient.
+
+Also: `test_defect_rate_and_competence_provenance_2026-08-23.py::
+test_nothing_imports_either_script_into_the_runner` pins this script RECORD ONLY.
+Promoting it to a gate overturns a pinned design decision and the proposal must say so.
+
+## On the construct (open question 1) — as a replacement, the continuous rate is worse
+
+Exp 42 measured the ladder's own construct: residual resolution on a fixed set, 0 of 7
+weak / 6 of 7 rung 1 / 7 of 7 by rung 2. A provenance-clean confirm rate measures a
+related but different construct. Under the additive standard a measurement of the wrong
+construct cannot displace a committed measurement of the right one, and "the shadow
+ranking does not distort" is the wrong promotion criterion — distortion-freedom in
+shadow is not evidence of predictive validity. Promotion should require the rate to
+predict fixed-residual resolution better than a re-run of the probe predicts itself.
+
+## On open question 3 — do NOT bundle with `immune_memory_enabled`
+
+Shared Beta-Binomial machinery is a convenience, not a demonstrated advantage. The
+founder's composability standard requires a *measurement* showing the composed work
+dominates each piece alone. None exists. Bundle only after one does.
+
+## A defect in the repair the simulated runner received tonight
+
+`routing_max_rungs=4` was added to `bench/tools/run_simulated_experiment.py` so that
+"6 of 6 source seats get a climb between two different models". Two measured problems.
+
+**Parity.** 0 of 288 config-shaped JSON files in this tree pin `routing_max_rungs`, so
+every real run uses the default of 2 and rungs 3–4 are structurally unreachable in every
+run the simulation is compared against. The literal sat immediately above a block headed
